09-20.md` sections 10-12 and the beads epic `forge-plugin-4g68`.\n    13\t\n    14\tStatus: **session brief, operator-issued 2026-09-23, for Fable sessions running the\n    15\trefactor-python plugin 0.1.3 in forge-plugin worktrees while the operator is away.** The shared\n    16\tprotocol is docs/analysis/refactor-plan-2026-09-19.md; where this brief narrows it (unattended\n    17\tstop rules, worktree layout, concurrency guards, the three plugin deviations in section 11) this\n    18\tbrief wins for these three sessions only. Where it conflicts with AGENTS.md / CLAUDE.md the\n    19\tcommitted rules govern.\n    20\t\n    21\t## 0. What this batch is and why\n    22\t\n    23\tThree test-file splits from the plan's order, chosen because nothing in the model-routing chains\n    24\t(docs/analysis/model-routing-implementation-plan-2026-09-22.md) edits them before chain J, and\n    25\tbecause none is an FR-230 subject, so there is no mint and no byte pin to chase:\n    26\t\n    27\t| Lane | Session | Bead | Target (code lines at 69bc28d) | Big class | Focused set at 69bc28d |\n    28\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n    29\t| A | 4 | forge-plugin-6g67 | tests/test_revision9_coordination.py (13,222) | Revision9BuilderBatchTests, 147 methods (109 tests, 38 helpers) | 144 tests, 22 s |\n    30\t| B1 | 8 | forge-plugin-25ms | tests/test_revision8_coordination.py (4,905) | Revision8CoordinationTests, 112 methods (81 tests, 31 helpers) | 81 tests, 35..46 s |\n    31\t| B2 | 6 | forge-plugin-kzu0 | tests/test_revision9_cli_surfaces.py (5,456) | Revision9BoundCLIIntegrationTests, 77 methods (62 tests, 15 helpers) | 85 tests, 109 s |\n    32\t\n    33\tTwo Fable sessions run at once: lane A does session 4; lane B does session 8 and, when its\n    34\thandover bead exists, session 6 in a fresh worktree from the same main tip. At most two refactor\n    35\tworktrees exist at any time, and never more than one Gate 1 cell runs on the host (section 6).\n    36\t\n    37\tOperator decisions recorded here (the sessions cite this brief instead of asking):\n    38\t\n    39\t1. The bead dependency edges 6g67 -> 37fr (closed), pot9 -> 6g67, kzu0 -> pot9, tyud -> kzu0,\n    40\t   25ms -> tyud are ordering suggestions from 2026-09-19. For this batch 6g67, 25ms and kzu0 are\n    41\t   released to run now and in parallel. Do not edit the dependency graph; note the release in the\n    42\t   first bead comment.\n    43\t2. Dropped from the batch, do not start them: the archive-run.py façade half of sweep-1 (the\n    44\t   split-module inventory at 69bc28d shows 171 top-level symbols, one dominant component of 119 of\n    45\t   124 defs after 12 hubs, a `global` statement, and the plugin has no façade mode; that needs a\n    46\t   planner and an operator, not an unattended night), sessions 5 and 7 (FR-230 test subjects,\n    47\t   id-identical mixin shape, re-mint), fresh_evals.py, chain_core, sweep-2, sweep-3.\n    48\t3. Each session stops at a pushed branch plus a handover bead. Reintegration through the Forge\n    49\t   worktree-merge chain is the operator's, in the morning, in the order the handover beads\n    50\t   were closed (B1, then B2, then A, smallest first so routing's V chain is not stuck behind the\n    51\t   13k-line merge).\n    52\t4. Every \"ask the operator\" in the plan, the skill and the session-2 brief becomes \"stop\" here\n    53\t   (section 8). There is nobody to ask. Never bypass, never widen, never hand-edit a body.\n    54\t\n    55\t## 1. Setup per lane (operator, before launch)\n    56\t\n    57\t**Layout (corrected twice: 01:25 after lane A's first stop, 11:30 for daytime).** Plugin enablement\n    58\tfor a git worktree is read from the repository's MAIN checkout's `.claude/settings.local.json`, not\n    59\tfrom the worktree's own file (verified 01:24: `claude plugin disable forge@forge --scope local` run\n    60\tinside a worktree wrote to the main checkout's file). So the switch is per repository, and the\n    61\trefactor lanes now live in a SEPARATE CLONE of the same GitHub remote:\n    62\t`/home/agents/foundry-of-zero/forge-plugin-refactor` (Forge off in its local settings, which its\n    63\town `info/exclude` hides) with one worktree per lane under\n    64\t`/home/agents/foundry-of-zero/forge-plugin-refactor-wt/<lane>`. The main clone\n    65\t`/home/agents/foundry-of-zero/forge-plugin` has Forge ON again for the routing and reintegration\n    66\tsessions; the lanes never touch it except through `bd -C` (its beads) and by reading this brief\n    67\tand the plan by absolute path. Branches are pushed to origin from the clone and reintegrated from\n    68\tthe main clone exactly as sessions 1 and 2 were. Each lane worktree's own\n    69\t`.claude/settings.local.json` carries the env block below. The harness does not pass `TMPDIR`\n    70\tfrom that block into the shell: every command that runs tests or gates exports\n    71\t`TMPDIR=/dev/shm/refactor-<lane>` itself. `REFACTOR_TYPE_CMD` points the gate's type step at the\n    72\tproduction package (section 11, item 3).\n    73\t\n    74\t```bash\n    75\t# lane A (session 4)\n    76\tcd /home/agents/foundry-of-zero/forge-plugin\n    77\tgit worktree add /home/agents/foundry-of-zero/forge-plugin-wt/s4 -b refactor/split-test-revision9-coordination main\n    78\tmkdir -p /home/agents/foundry-of-zero/forge-plugin-wt/s4/.claude /dev/shm/refactor-s4\n    79\tcat > /home/agents/foundry-of-zero/forge-plugin-wt/s4/.claude/settings.local.json <<'JSON'\n    80\t{\"enabledPlugins\": {\"forge@forge\": false},\n    81\t \"env\": {\"TMPDIR\": \"/dev/shm/refactor-s4\", \"PYTHONPATH\": \"scripts:scripts/forge\", \"MYPYPATH\": \"scripts:scripts/forge\",\n    82\t         \"REFACTOR_MAX_LINES\": \"1000\",\n    83\t         \"REFACTOR_TYPE_CMD\": \"mypy --no-error-summary --no-color-output --show-error-codes --hide-error-context scripts/forge/forge_cli\",\n    84\t         \"REFACTOR_TEST_CMD\": \"python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_revision9_coordination*.py'\"}}\n    85\tJSON\n    86\tcd /home/agents/foundry-of-zero/forge-plugin-wt/s4 && tmux new -d -s refactor-s4 \\\n    87\t  \"claude --plugin-dir /home/agents/foundry-of-zero/refactor-python --dangerously-skip-permissions \\\n    88\t   'Read /home/agents/foundry-of-zero/forge-plugin/docs/analysis/refactor-overnight-brief-2026-09-23.md and run lane A (session 4, bead forge-plugin-6g67) to its handover bead. Unattended: stop conditions in section 8.'\"\n    89\t```\n    90\t\n    91\t```bash\n    92\t# lane B (session 8 first; the session itself creates the s6 worktree afterwards, section 9)\n    93\tcd /home/agents/foundry-of-zero/forge-plugin\n    94\tgit worktree add /home/agents/foundry-of-zero/forge-plugin-wt/s8 -b refactor/split-test-revision8-coordination main\n    95\tmkdir -p /home/agents/foundry-of-zero/forge-plugin-wt/s8/.claude /dev/shm/refactor-s8\n    96\tcat > /home/agents/foundry-of-zero/forge-plugin-wt/s8/.claude/settings.local.json <<'JSON'\n    97\t{\"enabledPlugins\": {\"forge@forge\": false},\n    98\t \"env\": {\"TMPDIR\": \"/dev/shm/refactor-s8\", \"PYTHONPATH\": \"scripts:scripts/forge\", \"MYPYPATH\": \"scripts:scripts/forge\",\n    99\t         \"REFACTOR_MAX_LINES\": \"1000\",\n   100\t         \"REFACTOR_TYPE_CMD\": \"mypy --no-error-summary --no-color-output --show-error-codes --hide-error-context scripts/forge/forge_cli\",\n   101\t         \"REFACTOR_TEST_CMD\": \"python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -p 'test_revision8*.py'\"}}\n   102\tJSON\n   103\tcd /home/agents/foundry-of-zero/forge-plugin-wt/s8 && tmux new -d -s refactor-s8 \\\n   104\t  \"claude --plugin-dir /home/agents/foundry-of-zero/refactor-python --dangerously-skip-permissions \\\n   105\t   'Read /home/agents/foundry-of-zero/forge-plugin/docs/analysis/refactor-overnight-brief-2026-09-23.md and run lane B (session 8, bead forge-plugin-25ms, then session 6, bead forge-plugin-kzu0) to their handover beads. Unattended: stop conditions in section 8.'\"\n   106\t```\n   107\t\n   108\tMain clone facts at issue time: main = origin/main = 69bc28d; refactor-python is on branch\n   109\tplugin-0.1.3 at d265b57 (plugin.json version 0.1.3); codex-cli 0.155.1 authenticated;\n   110\t`bd` resolves the main clone's `.beads` from any worktree (verified with `bd context`); a\n   111\t`git worktree add ... main` plus the settings file leaves `git status` empty (verified).\n   112\tThe main clone carries staged, uncommitted routing docs; the worktrees branch from the `main`\n   113\tref and do not see them. Nothing in this brief touches the main clone's working tree.\n   114\t\n   115\t## 2. Read first, in this order\n   116\t\n   117\t1. `bd show <your bead>` including comments; docs/analysis/refactor-plan-2026-09-19.md sections\n   118\t   2, 3 and 5 (the progress log rows for sessions 1 and 2 carry the lessons).\n   119\t2. `bd recall refactor-session-operating-notes-2026-09-13`, `bd recall app-split-handoff-2026-09-18`,\n   120\t   `bd recall merge-engine-split-handoff-2026-09-22` (if present).\n   121\t3. The plugin's skills/decompose/SKILL.md and references/operations.md, in particular the\n   122\t   \"For test shapes\" and \"Real test files often define shared constants\" paragraphs; then\n   123\t   skills/split-module/SKILL.md phases 0, 1, 6 and 7 and its \"Rules that override everything\".\n   124\t4. docs/analysis/refactor-session-2-brief.md for the voice and the finalize/review shape\n   125\t   (historical; its FR-230 and annotate-self rules do not apply to test-only sessions).\n   126\t5. .refactor/plan-merge-engine.md and .refactor/critique-merge-engine.md as the planning\n   127\t   evidence format. Section 11 of this brief before planning: it lists what was verified\n   128\t   tonight and the three deviations you are allowed.\n   129\t\n   130\t## 3. Start checklist (run each, print each result; any failure is a stop)\n   131\t\n   132\t1. `pwd` is your lane's worktree; `git branch --show-current` is your lane's branch; `git log -1`\n   133\t   is 69bc28d or a later main tip (record it as BASE in `.refactor/`).\n   134\t2. `cat /home/agents/foundry-of-zero/forge-plugin/.claude/settings.local.json` (the MAIN clone's\n   135\t   file) shows `\"forge@forge\": false`; no `forge:*` skill is listed in this session; `env | grep -E\n   136\t   'PYTHONPATH|MYPYPATH|REFACTOR_'` shows the five values and you export `TMPDIR` yourself;\n   137\t   `FORGE_SESSION_PID` is unset. No `/forge:*` skill, chain, marker or approval in this session.\n   138\t   A plain commit works because the Forge commit guard is that plugin's hook. If a `forge:*`\n   139\t   skill is listed anyway, stop before the first commit (section 8).\n   140\t3. `bash $S/preflight.sh --decompose` reports no missing REQUIRED tool\n   141\t   ($S = /home/agents/foundry-of-zero/refactor-python/skills/split-module/scripts,\n   142\t   $D = /home/agents/foundry-of-zero/refactor-python/skills/decompose/scripts).\n   143\t4. `.refactor-quality.json` present (module_target 500, module_ceiling 1000, function_target 150,\n   144\t   class_target 30, max_parameters 6). `.refactor-baseline.json` has your source file's entry.\n   145\t5. Baseline green: `$REFACTOR_TEST_CMD` passes on the untouched branch and collects the expected\n   146\t   count (lane A 144, B1 81, B2 85). Record the wall time. (`discover -t . -s tests` is refused\n   147\t   by unittest because `tests/` has no `__init__.py`; the `-s tests` form is the one that works.)\n   148\t6. Test-ID freeze: `python3 $D/collect_tests.py snapshot --start tests --out .refactor/tests-<name>-before.json`.\n   149\t   The auto preset resolves to the namespace layout (top = `tests`, IDs like\n   150\t   `test_revision8_coordination.Revision8CoordinationTests.test_x`; 1,908 unittest and 1,908\n   151\t   pytest IDs at 69bc28d, about 5 s). `--top .` and `--preset package` are refused for the same\n   152\t   reason as item 5; do not try to force them. Never change the preset between snapshots.\n   153\t7. Source freeze for the manifest oracle: `python3 $S/snapshot_bodies.py snapshot tests --out\n   154\t   .refactor/before-<name>.json` (2,906 bodies, 4 s). The gate `--pkg` for a test-only session\n   155\t   is `tests`; the oracle refuses a manifest whose touched files lie outside the compared scope,\n   156\t   so every per-cluster snapshot and compare uses `tests` too.\n   157\t8. Gate dry run on the clean tree: `bash $S/verify.sh --pkg tests --snapshot .refactor/before-<name>.json\n   158\t   --strict-bodies --fast` prints PASS for compile, ruff-lint, file-length, types,\n   159\t   import-contracts and bodies-unchanged (5 s at 69bc28d with the env of section 1).\n   160\t9. Commit the freeze evidence as the branch's first commit.\n   161\t\n   162\t`<name>` is `revision8`, `revision9-cli` or `revision9-coord`. Every evidence file goes under\n   163\ttracked `.refactor/` with a unique name carrying `<name>`; the movers refuse evidence paths\n   164\toutside the project, and nothing in `$TMPDIR` or the scratchpad is evidence.\n   165\t\n   166\t## 4. The shape recipe (identical for the three targets)\n   167\t\n   168\tFour kinds of commits, in this order, each its own commit and (from the third on) its own\n   169\tmanifest:\n   170\t\n   171\t1. **Config-only prep, before any move** (session-2 lesson): pyproject.toml\n   172\t   `[tool.ruff.lint.per-file-ignores]` gains two temporary globs, `\"tests/test_<stem>_*.py\"` and\n   173\t   `\"tests/_<name>_*.py\"`, whose list is the source file's current entry (pyproject lines 242,\n   174\t   244, 245) MINUS `I001`; plus provisional `.refactor-baseline.json` entries for every planned\n   175\t   module over 500 (added once the plan is approved, still before the first family cluster).\n   176\t   **Operator ruling 2026-09-23 11:30 on both lanes' stop finding (import bootstrap order):** the\n   177\t   same config-only prep, in a commit that precedes the mixin commit, adds\n   178\t