replaces the globs with measured per-module\n   202\t   entries and deletes them.\n   203\t2. **Preamble prerequisites into a constants module** (the inventory names them, section 5).\n   204\t   `rope_move.py` cannot do this here (section 11, item 1), so this is the one hand-written\n   205\t   preparation commit of the session: create `tests/_<name>_constants.py` containing the\n   206\t   named top-level statements verbatim (same text, same order, keeping `ROOT =\n   207\t   Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]`, which resolves to the same repo root from that path),\n   208\t   the imports they need, and a copy of the source's `sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT / \"scripts\"))`\n   209\t   line when the source has one (so the support module's copied `codex_orchestrator` import\n   210\t   resolves without PYTHONPATH); delete those statements from the source and add one line\n   211\t   `from tests._<name>_constants import <names>` at the position of the first removed statement\n   212\t   (before the source's own `sys.path.insert`, so `ROOT` is bound for it). No other line of the\n   213\t   source changes. Verify: `ruff check` clean on both files, `$REFACTOR_TEST_CMD` green, and\n   214\t   `git diff` shows only removed statements plus the one import. Re-collect IDs (identity\n   215\t   compare against the freeze) and re-freeze the source snapshot after this commit.\n   216\t3. **Helpers into a support mixin**. `python3 $D/move_methods.py --project . --import-root \"$PWD\"\n   217\t   --source tests/<file> --class <BigClass> --methods <setUp plus every non-test_ helper>\n   218\t   --dest tests/_<name>_support.py --shape mixin --target-class <Name>Support --test-only\n   219\t   --test-snapshot .refactor/tests-<name>-<n>.json --format-imports --manifest\n   220\t   .refactor/mixin-<name>.json`, dry run (inspect the diff: the source gains\n   221\t   `from tests._<name>_support import <Name>Support` and the class header becomes\n   222\t   `class <BigClass>(<Name>Support, <original bases>)`; the destination gains the helpers\n   223\t   verbatim, the imports they own, and `from tests._<name>_constants import ...`), then\n   224\t   `--apply`. `--import-root \"$PWD\"` is required (section 11, item 2): with the default the\n   225\t   mover writes a bare `from _<name>_support import`, which the Gate 1 cell cannot import.\n   226\t   The mixin's name must not contain `Test`; decorated helpers (`property`, `contextmanager`,\n   227\t   `staticmethod`) travel verbatim in this shape. The mixin cannot live in the constants module\n   228\t   (section 11, item 4). Gate with `--test-mode identity`. After the commit also run\n   229\t   `env -u PYTHONPATH python3 -m unittest tests.<module>` once: it proves the `sys.path` line\n   230\t   in the constants module does its job.\n   231\t4. **Scenario families in class shape**, one commit per family: `python3 $D/move_methods.py\n   232\t   --project . --import-root \"$PWD\" --source tests/<file> --class <BigClass> --methods <tests of\n   233\t   the family> --dest tests/test_<stem>_<family>.py --shape class --target-class <Family>Tests\n   234\t   --test-only --test-snapshot <ids> --id-map .refactor/idmap-<name>-<family>.json\n   235\t   --format-imports --manifest .refactor/family-<name>-<family>.json`. The id map is a JSON\n   236\t   object `{\"unittest\": {old: new}, \"pytest\": {old: new}}` covering exactly the moved tests in\n   237\t   both collectors (old IDs from the current snapshot; new IDs substitute the module and class).\n   238\t   The sibling class copies the source class's bases (support mixin first, then the original\n   239\t   base), so the helpers are inherited; a dry run before the mixin commit is refused with\n   240\t   \"sibling class would lose calls to remaining methods\", which is the designed order check.\n   241\t   New modules are named `tests/test_revision8_<family>.py`,\n   242\t   `tests/test_revision9_coordination_<family>.py`, `tests/test_revision9_cli_surfaces_<family>.py`\n   243\t   so the lane's `REFACTOR_TEST_CMD` pattern, the ruff glob and the Gate 1 cell's\n   244\t   `tests/test_*.py` glob all pick them up; class names end in `Tests` like the source so pytest\n   245\t   collects them too (both collectors must map 1:1). Gate with `--test-mode mapping`.\n   246\t\n   247\tPlanning rules the critic enforces (a plan that breaks one is rejected, not ruled over):\n   248\t\n   249\t- Families are the inventory's clusters after hub peeling, merged to 500..1,000 code lines per\n   250\t  module and named after the scenario (the bead: \"planner names them\"). A plan with any module\n   251\t  over 1,000 is rejected at critique: split the family.\n   252\t- The source module keeps: the classes that were never in scope (lane B2: eight classes;\n   253\t  lane A: Revision9FixtureTests, Revision9BindingTests 2,125 lines and\n   254\t  Revision9MergeTransitionGrammarTests 2,777 lines are separate classes and separate targets of\n   255\t  the same session if the plan reaches them; section 5), the shell of the big class with\n   256\t  whatever the mover refuses (lane A: the one `unittest.skipUnless`-decorated test, verdict\n   257\t  \"unsupported: unknown decorator\", stays in the source class), and `if __name__ == \"__main__\"`\n   258\t  if present.\n   259\t- Every mover call has `--format-imports` (the repository enforces isort). No `I001` in any\n   260\t  destination per-file ignore.\n   261\t- Never hand-edit a body, a docstring, a decorator or an assertion. The only hand-written\n   262\t  commit is item 2 above. Layout pins would be repointed in the same commit as a move under\n   263\t  the operator's standing permission, but the census found none on these three files (0 sites),\n   264\t  so any test failure that is not a collection or import error is a stop, not a repoint.\n   265\t- No production file changes in these sessions. `git diff --stat BASE..HEAD -- scripts docs/specs\n   266\t  .forge` must be empty at every commit. Therefore no mint, no byte pin, no spec sentence.\n   267\t- `__all__` does not exist in these files; do not create one. CHANGELOG: one `[Unreleased]`\n   268\t  entry per branch at finalize, in the style of the MergeEngine entry, shorter, naming the\n   269\t  hand-written constants commit and the `--import-root` deviation.\n   270\t\n   271\t## 5. Per-target facts (class_inventory.py at 69bc28d, tonight)\n   272\t\n   273\t**Lane B1, Revision8CoordinationTests** (tests/test_revision8_coordination.py, lines 28..end,\n   274\tone class): 112 methods, 109 ok, 3 wrap (`runs_root` and `registry_path` properties,\n   275\t`api_environment` contextmanager: they move in the helper mixin, not function shape).\n   276\tPrerequisites: `ROOT` (line 18), `TOOLS` (line 19, 2 users) and `RECORDED_AT` (line 25, 25\n   277\tusers); the source keeps reading `ROOT` for its own `sys.path.insert`. Verified tonight on a\n   278\tthrowaway worktree: with `tests/_revision8_constants.py` holding those three statements and the\n   279\tsource importing them, the mixin dry run of all 31 helpers verifies clean; the destination\n   280\theader is `from codex_orchestrator import batch, journal` plus `from tests._revision8_constants\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
