\n     5\\t  },\\n     6\\t  \\\"hooks\\\": {\\n     7\\t    \\\"SessionStart\\\": [\\n     8\\t      {\\n     9\\t        \\\"matcher\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    10\\t        \\\"hooks\\\": [\\n    11\\t          {\\n    12\\t            \\\"type\\\": \\\"command\\\",\\n    13\\t            \\\"command\\\": \\\"mkdir -p /dev/shm/forge-gate && chmod 700 /dev/shm/forge-gate && find /dev/shm/forge-gate -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -mmin +180 -exec rm -rf {} + 2>/dev/null; true\\\"\\n    14\\t          }\\n    15\\t        ]\\n    16\\t      }\\n    17\\t    ]\\n    18\\t  },\\n    19\\t  \\\"enabledPlugins\\\": {\\n    20\\t\\t\\\"forge@forge\\\": false\\n    21\\t}\\n    22\\t}\\n     1\\t# Refactor plan — 2026-09-19\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\tPoint of reference for the decomposition sessions that work through\\n     4\\t`refactoring-candidates-2026-09-19.md`. Measured on main 7e40590. One session per target,\\n     5\\tone branch per session, one Forge reintegration per branch. Beads carry the per-target\\n     6\\tinstructions; this document carries the shared protocol and the order. The beads are\\n     7\\tchained as dependencies in plan order, so `bd ready` surfaces the next session; sweep-1\\n     8\\t(forge-plugin-i5od) is deliberately unchained because it may run in parallel with session 2.\\n     9\\t\\n    10\\tPlugin: `~/foundry-of-zero/refactor-python`, tag 0.1.0 plus the `plain_decorators` change\\n    11\\t(commit and tag 0.1.1 before session 1). Loaded with `claude --plugin-dir ~/foundry-of-zero/refactor-python`\\n    12\\ton this machine. Its hooks (a SessionStart notice and a PostToolUse file-length check) are\\n    13\\tsession-scoped by `--plugin-dir`; nothing is installed into this repository and nothing needs\\n    14\\tremoving afterwards.\\n    15\\t\\n    16\\t## 1. Targets and sizes\\n    17\\t\\n    18\\tTwo numbers, both in code lines as `scripts/check_file_length.py` counts them:\\n    19\\t\\n    20\\t- **Target 500** per module. The planner plans to it. This is the repository budget.\\n    21\\t- **Ceiling 1,000** for any module a session creates. A module between 500 and 1,000 needs\\n    22\\t  a provisional entry in `.refactor-baseline.json` (the repository guard still enforces 500)\\n    23\\t  and a row in the session's debt report with a reason and a follow-up bead. A plan that\\n    24\\t  creates a module over 1,000 is rejected at critique.\\n    25\\t- Functions over 150 lines and classes over 30 methods stay listed as candidates in the\\n    26\\t  debt report even when their module fits.\\n    27\\t\\n    28\\tConfigured in `.refactor-quality.json` (tracked; commit it with session 1):\\n    29\\t\\n    30\\t```json\\n    31\\t{\\\"module_target\\\": 500, \\\"module_ceiling\\\": 1000, \\\"function_target\\\": 150, \\\"class_target\\\": 30,\\n    32\\t \\\"max_parameters\\\": 6, \\\"plain_decorators\\\": [\\\"_serialize_worktree_command\\\"]}\\n    33\\t```\\n    34\\t\\n    35\\t`plain_decorators` declares the project's own function-wrapper decorator so that Engine's\\n    36\\t18 verb methods are movable; a function-shape move re-applies it in the class binding.\\n    37\\t\\n    38\\t## 2. Session protocol\\n    39\\t\\n    40\\t### Start checklist (the session runs these, the bead tells it to)\\n    41\\t\\n    42\\t1. `cat .claude/settings.local.json` shows `\\\"forge@forge\\\": false`. If not, set it and note it\\n    43\\t   for the end checklist. No `/forge:*` skills, chains, markers or approvals during the session.\\n    44\\t2. `git status` clean on `main` at the tip named in the bead; `git switch -c refactor/<name>`.\\n    45\\t3. `bash $S/preflight.sh --decompose` reports no missing REQUIRED tool (LibCST, rope, ruff, mypy, pytest).\\n    46\\t4. `.refactor-quality.json` present with the values above.\\n    47\\t5. Environment exported in the launching shell (they die with the shell, nothing to remove):\\n    48\\t   `REFACTOR_TEST_CMD=\\\"python3 -m unittest <focused modules from the bead>\\\"`,\\n    49\\t   `REFACTOR_MINT_CMD=\\\"python3 .codex-orchestrator/runs/run-20260906-95e4-phase3/evidence/mint.py\\\"`,\\n    50\\t   `TMPDIR=/dev/shm/forge-gate`, `FORGE_SESSION_PID` unset.\\n    51\\t6. Baseline green: the focused set passes on the untouched branch; the gate-1 cell (4 shards)\\n    52\\t   was green on the named main tip.\\n    53\\t7. Read: beads memory `refactor-session-operating-notes-2026-09-13`, `app-split-handoff-2026-09-18`;\\n    54\\t   the plugin's `skills/decompose/SKILL.md` and `references/operations.md` (or `split-module`\\n    55\\t   for pure-move targets); the target bead.\\n    56\\t\\n    57\\t### During\\n    58\\t\\n    59\\t- Freeze (bodies, test ids where tests are touched, type baseline), inventory, plan, critique,\\n    60\\t  then one cluster at a time, sequential per source file. Dry run, then `--apply`, always with\\n    61\\t  `--format-imports` (this repository enforces isort).\\n    62\\t- Never hand-edit a body. A refusal is a planning result: re-plan or report, never bypass.\\n    63\\t- Tier 1 (relocation) and tier 2 (declared extraction) never share a commit. Tier 3 is not\\n    64\\t  in this plan.\\n    65\\t- FR-230: production subjects are byte-pinned. Add every new module under a subject package\\n    66\\t  to the manifest, run `verify.sh --mint` at wave close and finalize, commit the manifest,\\n    67\\t  `tests/fixtures/fr230-results/*.json` and the byte pin with the wave. Keep the digest tests\\n    68\\t  out of the focused per-cluster set.\\n    69\\t- Layout pins (patch targets, `__globals__` identity, plain assignments in fixtures) are\\n    70\\t  repointed in the same commit as the move under the operator's standing permission.\\n    71\\t  Behaviour tests are never edited. Class-patch sites keep working under function-shape\\n    72\\t  bindings and need no repoint; confirm with the census output.\\n    73\\t- `__all__` verbatim from baseline to finalize. CHANGELOG: one entry per branch.\\n    74\\t\\n    75\\t### End checklist\\n    76\\t\\n    77\\t1. Finalize: measured `.refactor-baseline.json` (old entry gone or shrunk, provisional\\n    78\\t   entries only for modules the plan marked over target), `lint-imports` contract, spec\\n    79\\t   line 117 wording if a package layout changed, re-mint, gate-1 cell twice consecutively.\\n    80\\t2. Codex review detached, then the Fable reviewer adjudicates; consensus round on disagreement.\\n    81\\t3. Debt report: every module between 500 and 1,000, every function over 150 lines, every\\n    82\\t   class over 30 methods, each with reason and follow-up bead.\\n    83\\t4. Handover bead in the style of forge-plugin-90b0: branch, tip SHA, old-to-new path map,\\n    84\\t   every non-move edit, expected gates, debt report. Push the branch. Reintegration is a\\n    85\\t   separate Forge session.\\n    86\\t5. Restore `.claude/settings.local.json` to `\\\"forge@forge\\\": true`. Remove the run's\\n    87\\t   worktrees and branches. The exported environment ends with the shell.\\n    88\\t\\n    89\\t## 3. Order\\n    90\\t\\n    91\\t| # | Target | Bead | Tool and shape | Notes |\\n    92\\t|---|---|---|---|---|\\n    93\\t| 1 | `forge_cli/engine/_engine.py` (3,574; Engine, 41 methods) | forge-plugin-321p | decompose, function shape, manual phases (not the workflow) | First real decompose run; the operator watches the first cluster through gate and merge. |\\n    94\\t| 2 | `forge_cli/app/_merge_engine.py` (10,302; MergeEngine, 93 methods) | forge-plugin-37fr | decompose workflow, function shape, seven seams, then tier 2 on the eight methods over 250 lines | Depends on 1. Largest context and parallel-editing win. |\\n    95\\t| 3 | sweep-1: `fresh_evals.py`, `archive-run.py` façade, `batch.py` if not vendored | forge-plugin-i5od | split-module (pure moves) | May run in parallel with 2 in a second worktree; reintegrations stay sequential. |\\n    96\\t| 4 | `tests/test_revision9_coordination.py` (13,222) | forge-plugin-6g67 | decompose, class shape (ids unpinned), preamble prep first | Largest test file. |\\n    97\\t| 5 | `tests/test_cli_merge_integration.py` (7,332) | forge-plugin-pot9 | decompose, mixin shape (shard suite, FR-230 test subject) | Ids and shard membership must be identical. |\\n    98\\t| 6 | `tests/test_revision9_cli_surfaces.py` (5,456) | forge-plugin-kzu0 | decompose, class shape | |\\n    99\\t| 7 | `tests/test_cli_merge_lifecycle.py` (4,946) | forge-plugin-tyud | decompose, mixin shape (FR-230 test subject) | |\\n   100\\t| 8 | `tests/test_revision8_coordination.py` (4,905) | forge-plugin-25ms | decompose, class shape | |\\n143-   143\\t```\\n144-   144\\t<!-- FORGE:REGION gate1-test-command END -->\\n145-   145\\t\\n146:   146\\t## Changelog Policy\\n147-   147\\t\\n148:   148\\t<!-- FORGE:REGION changelog-policy BEGIN -->\\n149:   149\\tA `CHANGELOG.md` in Keep a Changelog format is maintained at the repository root. A commit whose\\n150-   150\\tstaged paths touch the `python`, `bash`, `config`, or `control` categories requires at least one\\n151:   151\\tnew changelog entry line staged in the same candidate — normally under the `## [Unreleased]`\\n152-   152\\theading; a release commit instead moves the `[Unreleased]` body under the new version heading,\\n153:   153\\twhich the mechanical check deliberately also accepts. A commit whose\\n154-   154\\tstaged paths are exclusively docs-class (`docs/**`, `.forge/history/**`,\\n155-   155\\t`.forge/evals/candidates/**`, `*.md`/`*.txt` outside control locations, `UPSTREAM`, and\\n156-   156\\t`CHANGELOG.md` itself) is exempt. Release commits move the `[Unreleased]` body under the new\\n157:   157\\tversion heading. Archive-only chains skip this gate under the operator's standing direction of\\n158:   158\\t2026-08-31 (recorded per chain via `commit skip changelog`).\\n159-   159\\t\\n160-   160\\t```bash\\n161-   161\\tpython3 - \\\"$@\\\" <<'PY'\\n--\\n165-   165\\t\\n166-   166\\tpaths = sys.argv[1:]\\n167-   167\\tif not paths:\\n168:   168\\t    print(\\\"changelog gate: no target paths supplied\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n169-   169\\t    raise SystemExit(1)\\n170-   170\\t\\n171-   171\\tEXEMPT_PREFIXES = (\\\"docs/\\\", \\\".forge/history/\\\", \\\".forge/evals/candidates/\\\")\\n--\\n194-   194\\t\\n195-   195\\trequired = sorted(path for path in paths if requires_entry(path))\\n196-   196\\tif not required:\\n197:   197\\t    print(\\\"changelog gate: docs-class candidate, no entry required\\\")\\n198-   198\\t    raise SystemExit(0)\\n199-   199\\t\\n200-   200\\tdiff = subprocess.run(\\n--\\n202-   202\\t    capture_output=True, text=True, check=False,\\n203-   203\\t)\\n204-   204\\tif diff.returncode != 0:\\n205:   205\\t    print(\\\"changelog gate: git diff --cached failed\\\", file=sys.stderr)\\n206-   206\\t    raise SystemExit(1)\\n207-   207\\tadded_entries = [\\n208-   208\\t    line for line in diff.stdout.splitlines()\\n--\\n212-   212\\t    [\\\"git\\\", \\\"show\\\", \\\":CHANGELOG.md\\\"], capture_output=True, text=True, check=False,\\n213-   213\\t)\\n214-   214\\tif added_entries and staged.returncode == 0 and \\\"## [Unreleased]\\\" in staged.stdout:\\n215:   215\\t    print(f\\\"changelog gate: entry present for {len(required)} in-scope path(s)\\\")\\n216-   216\\t    raise SystemExit(0)\\n217-   217\\tprint(\\n218:   218\\t    \\\"changelog gate: staged candidate touches \\\"\\n219-   219\\t    + \\\", \\\".join(required[:5])\\n220-   220\\t    + (\\\" …\\\" if len(required) > 5 else \\\"\\\")\\n221-   221\\t    + \\\" but adds no CHANGELOG.md [Unreleased] entry\\\",\\n--\\n226-   226\\t```\\n227-   227\\t\\n228-   228\\tOutput path: `CHANGELOG.md`\\n229:   229\\t<!-- FORGE:REGION changelog-policy END -->\\n230-   230\\t\\n231-   231\\t## Review Prompt Project Focus\\n232-   232\\t\\n78d9610 chore(refactor): temporary ruff per-file-ignores glob for engine/_verbs_*.py (config-only)\\n CHANGELOG.md   | 1 +\\n pyproject.toml | 1 +\\n 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+)\\n813246a chore(engine): finalize the Engine decompose (measured ruff entries, size and type baselines, layer row, debt report)\\n .refactor-baseline.json                  |  3 +-\\n .refactor/debt-engine-class.md           | 50 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\\n .refactor/gate-engine-finalize-mint.txt  | 11 +++++++\\n .refactor/gate1-engine-finalize-run1.txt | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++\\n .refactor/gate1-engine-finalize-run2.txt | 33 +++++++++++++++++++++\\n .refactor/type-baseline.json             |  8 ++---\\n CHANGELOG.md                             |  2 +-\\n pyproject.toml                           | 13 +++++++--\\n 8 files changed, 143 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)\\n     1\\t# Changelog\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\tAll notable changes to the Forge plugin are documented in this file.\\n     4\\t\\n     5\\tThe format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),\\n     6\\tand this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).\\n     7\\tRelease dates are the UTC dates of the release commits.\\n     8\\t\\n     9\\t## [Unreleased]\\n    10\\t\\n    11\\t### Changed\\n    12\\t\\n    13\\t- Refactor (engine): the `Engine` class in `scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine/_engine.py` (3,574 code lines, 41 methods) is decomposed with the refactor-python `decompose` skill in function shape (bead forge-plugin-321p, plan `.refactor/plan-engine-class.md`): 33 verb-method bodies move verbatim (LibCST, manifest-verified AST oracle, `--strict-bodies`, one tier-1 cluster per commit) into nine modules — `_verbs_tombstone.py` (346 code lines), `_verbs_status.py` (275), `_verbs_lifecycle.py` (429), `_verbs_gate.py` (458), `_verbs_gate_evals.py` (377), `_verbs_decision.py` (327), `_verbs_review_request.py` (458), `_verbs_review_collect.py` (398), `_verbs_finalize.py` (395) — and `_engine.py` keeps the class shell (324 code lines: `__init__`, the hubs `select`, `_preflight`, `_wrong_state`, `next_step`, `_emit_decision`, the two helpers they call, and one `name = _verbs_<x>.name` binding per moved method, re-wrapped with `staticmethod` or `_serialize_worktree_command` exactly as before), so `Engine.<verb>` lookups, unbound `Engine._profiles_for_path`/`_parse_verdict` calls, `patch.object(Engine, ...)` and `inspect.getsource(Engine.gate_run)` are unchanged; no body, verb, diagnostic or reason-code byte changes; the engine package root and its `__all__` are byte-identical. The nine modules are FR-230 production subjects (re-minted); `pyproject.toml` gains one measured ruff per-file-ignores entry per verb module (the temporary `_verbs_*.py` glob that carried `_engine.py`'s grandfathered codes during the moves is gone), the `_engine.py` entry shrinks to the five codes it still trips, a `forge_cli.engine layers` row places the verb modules under `_engine`, the `_engine.py` size-baseline entry (3574) is deleted, and the mypy ratchet drops 251 -> 241 (ten grandfathered checks inside moved bodies no longer fire because a moved function's `self` is untyped; tracked as debt with a follow-up bead).\\n    14\\t- Refactor: `scripts/forge/forge_cli/app.py` (11,524 lines) becomes the `forge_cli.app` package — a root `__init__.py` with the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports plus five submodules moved by rope under the AST body oracle (bead forge-plugin-hcuo, plan `.refactor/plan-app.md`): `_mutation_journal.py`, `_admission.py`, `_candidate_observation.py`, `_merge_engine.py` (the `MergeEngine` class, the one new over-budget size-baseline entry at its measured count under the operator ruling on that bead; its class split is a follow-up) and `_dispatch.py`. One non-move edit rides with it: tests patch app-layer controls through one `patch_app` loader helper (E0; the loader sweep rejects raw module patches on app aliases). No body, verb, diagnostic, reason code or `--help` byte changes; the spec's package sentence, the FR-230 production subjects (re-minted), per-module ruff ignores and a `forge_cli.app layers` import-linter contract follow.\\n    15\\t- Refactor: `scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine.py` (12,178 lines) becomes the `forge_cli.engine` package — a root `__init__.py` with the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports plus 29 submodules moved by rope under the AST body oracle (bead forge-plugin-2fc, plan `.refactor/plan-engine.md`). Two non-move edits ride with it: the merge bootstrap child resolves `scripts/forge/cli.py` from `runtime.py`'s location instead of its own file depth (E1, with a focused test), and tests patch engine controls through one `patch_engine` loader helper (E0; the hermetic chain fixture assigns the codex executable on every engine module that binds it). The reviewer-facing eval trigger table names `scripts/forge/forge_cli/engine/**` in place of `engine.py` in the spec, the policy constant, the rendered project files and the fixtures; the Revision-9 seam-marker loop moves from the `chain_core` package root to `_commit_chain.py` beside `register_coordination_seams` (bead forge-plugin-4j7, finding CON-02; its grandfathered size entry rises 1840 -> 1847 by operator direction of 2026-09-17); the FR-230 production subjects are the engine package files, re-minted; the size baseline is re-pinned at measured sizes (`engine/_engine.py`, the `Engine` class, is the one new over-budget entry), the ruff per-file ignores are narrowed per engine module, and an import-linter layers contract locks the package's wave order.\\n    16\\t- Test isolation (beads forge-plugin-0eq, forge-plugin-ehn): `tests/test_audit_commitments.py` writes its disabled-control mutants of `audit-commitments.py` under a private temp directory (pinning the script's plugin root) instead of beside the real script, so a parallel Gate 1 shard copying the tracked `scripts/` tree no longer races on a vanishing sibling; `tests/test_mutation_runner.py` sets `FORGE_SESSION_PID` to the test process for the runner child instead of inheriting the caller's value, so an exported session identity no longer fails ten tests with a foreign-live-owner refusal.\\n    17\\t- chain_core split follow-ups (bead forge-plugin-r0b; review-final findings at reintegration): `scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/_state.py` declares its constants in the historical module order again (bodies unchanged; FR-230 manifest, result fixtures and the v2 byte pin re-minted for the changed production subject); the spec's package sentence names the submodules by the FR-230 manifest's production-subject list instead of the planning document; `pyproject.toml` per-file-ignores drop the dead `chain_core.py` entry and the blanket `chain_core/**` glob in favour of one entry per submodule listing only the codes it trips, and `scripts/check_file_length.py` is cleaned to the full rule set (its entry removed) and gains a focused unittest (`tests/test_check_file_length.py`: hook and plain-mode exit codes, the exact guard diagnostic, and an in-memory control-disable leg); `import-linter==2.15` is pinned beside ruff in the guardrails workflow and the pre-commit setup line. Disclosure: the 0.6.12 reintegration's `.claude/settings.json` also carries `worktree.baseRef: head` and `enabledPlugins: codex-orchestrator@codex-orchestrator` (operator-approved at Gate 4 on 2026-09-14; the plugin entry dangles on a clone without that marketplace). Deferred to the `_commit_chain` split (bead forge-plugin-4j7): moving the Revision-9 seam-marker loop out of the package root, because the grandfathered `_commit_chain.py` may not grow.\\n    18\\t- Reviewer-facing eval fixture `review-passes-clean-change` is brought up to the conventions it claims to follow (first fresh-reviewer-evals run since the chain_core split's guardrails landed): its test imports are in the order the ruff I001 gate requires and its diff carries the `CHANGELOG.md` entry the changelog policy requires for added Python files; expected verdict unchanged (PASS). Landed as its own commit because a candidate may not rewrite an established fixture that judges it (bead forge-plugin-r0b).\\n    19\\t- Refactor (chain_core): `scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core.py` (about 19,300 code lines) is now the package `scripts/forge/forge_cli/chain_core/`: 45 submodules hold the 315 moved symbols with every function and class body unchanged (strict AST oracle 881/881), and the root `__init__.py` keeps the verbatim `__all__` and re-exports every symbol the module defined, so `forge_cli.chain_core.<name>` and the CLI shim's forwarding are unchanged. Unused imports are no longer bound on the package root; test patches of moved controls go through `tests/_cli_loader.patch_chain_core`, which patches every submodule binding the name. The spec's package sentence, the size baseline (eight over-budget chain_core files recorded at measured size) and a `forge_cli.chain_core layers` import-linter contract follow (bead forge-plugin-deb; follow-ups in forge-plugin-r0b and forge-plugin-4j7).\\n    20\\t- File categories: `*.js` now belongs to the `config` category (and the changelog gate's code-suffix list), so a tracked JavaScript file such as the chain_core split's Workflow script `.refactor/split-chain-core.workflow.js` matches a category and `tests.test_repo_conformance` file-category coverage passes (bead forge-plugin-g9i).\\n    21\\t- Review evidence for the chain_core split is tracked under `.refactor/`: the Codex review transcripts (`codex-review.jsonl`, `codex-review-chain_core.jsonl`, thread `01a0a015-b9f3-7072-9abd-4d4a29f96082`) and their verdict summaries (`codex-review.md`, `codex-review-chain_core.md`), cited by the handback on bead forge-plugin-deb. Evidence only; no runtime surface changes.\\n    22\\t\\n    23\\t## [0.6.12] - 2026-09-13\\n    24\\t\\n    25\\t### Changed\\n    26\\t\\n    27\\t- Run-bound commit chains no longer freeze at a multi-cell stack gate (GH#23). A stack-validations region with two or more fenced cells recorded one bound journal verification per cell while the replay validator required the whole batch, so `verify` returned `frozen-chain — carried binding fact is stale` after the first cell. The engine now emits one passed bound verification per completed batch, sourced from the final cell; a failed cell still records its failure immediately and stops the batch. Per-cell chain facts, the currentness predicate and non-run-bound chains are unchanged. FR-230 evidence re-minted.\\n    28\\t\\n    29\\t## [0.6.11] - 2026-09-11\\n    30\\t\\n    31\\t### Changed\\n    32\\t\\n    33\\t- Stack-validations grammar legibility (bead forge-plugin-28y, GH#12(f), GH#19): a\\n    34\\t  committed Stack Validations region that is present but holds no fenced shell cell\\n    35\\t  (the prose shape `/forge:init` 0.6.x emitted) now refuses with its own literal naming\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n/home/agents/foundry-of-zero/forge-plugin/.refactor/consensus-engine-class-B3.jsonl:6:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"agent_message\",\"text\":\"AGREE\\n\\n`.claude/settings.local.json:19-20` disables `forge@forge`, while `docs/analysis/refactor-plan-2026-09-19.md:42-43` explicitly prohibits Forge chains during the split, line 73 requires “CHANGELOG: one entry per branch,” and lines 83-85 defer Forge reintegration to a separate session. `git show --stat 78d9610` confirms the branch entry was added with the setup commit, and `git show 813246a:CHANGELOG.md | nl -ba` shows the finalized entry at line 13. Thus the cluster commits complied with the governing branch protocol; their conflict with `.refactor/plan-engine-class.md` should be disclosed as an advisory, not treated as a blocking gate failure.\"}}\n.refactor/codex-review-revision9-cli.jsonl:90:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_44\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \\\"nl -ba docs/analysis/refactor-plan-2026-09-19.md | sed -n '55,110p'\\nrg -n \\\\\\\"Tier 1|Tier 2|manifest|unmanifested|preparation\\\\\\\" docs/analysis/refactor-session-2-brief.md docs/analysis/refactor-plan-2026-09-19.md .refactor/plan-merge-engine.md | sed -n '1,260p'\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"    55\\tin step 5 lives under `.codex-orchestrator/runs/`, which is per-clone (`info/exclude`) — the\\n    56\\tchecklist is reproducible only on a machine that holds that run directory.\\n    57\\t\\n    58\\t1. `cat .claude/settings.local.json` shows `\\\"forge@forge\\\": false`. If not, set it and note it\\n    59\\t   for the end checklist. No `/forge:*` skills, chains, markers or approvals during the session.\\n    60\\t2. `git status` clean on `main` at the tip named in the bead; `git switch -c refactor/<name>`.\\n    61\\t3. `bash $S/preflight.sh --decompose` reports no missing REQUIRED tool (LibCST, rope, ruff, mypy, pytest).\\n    62\\t4. `.refactor-quality.json` present with the values above.\\n    63\\t5. Environment exported in the launching shell (they die with the shell, nothing to remove):\\n    64\\t   `REFACTOR_TEST_CMD=\\\"python3 -m unittest <focused modules from the bead>\\\"`,\\n    65\\t   `REFACTOR_MINT_CMD=\\\"python3 .codex-orchestrator/runs/run-20260906-95e4-phase3/evidence/mint.py\\\"`,\\n    66\\t   `PYTHONPATH=scripts:scripts/forge`, `MYPYPATH=scripts:scripts/forge`,\\n    67\\t   `TMPDIR=/dev/shm/forge-gate`, `FORGE_SESSION_PID` unset.\\n    68\\t6. Baseline green: the focused set passes on the untouched branch; the gate-1 cell (4 shards)\\n    69\\t   was green on the named main tip.\\n    70\\t7. Read: beads memory `refactor-session-operating-notes-2026-09-13`, `app-split-handoff-2026-09-18`;\\n    71\\t   the plugin's `skills/decompose/SKILL.md` and `references/operations.md` (or `split-module`\\n    72\\t   for pure-move targets); the target bead.\\n    73\\t\\n    74\\t### During\\n    75\\t\\n    76\\t- Freeze (bodies, test ids where tests are touched, type baseline), inventory, plan, critique,\\n    77\\t  then one cluster at a time, sequential per source file. Dry run, then `-