es:\n    77\t\n    78\t- `forge-project.md`\n    79\t- `.forge-manifest`\n    80\t- `.codex/**`\n    81\t- `.forge/evals/tasks/**`, including baselines\n    82\t- `AGENTS.md`\n    83\t- `CLAUDE.md`\n    84\t- `.claude/settings*.json`\n    85\t- `.github/workflows/**`, or equivalent CI configuration paths recorded in `file-categories`\n    86\t\n    87\tProject configuration may extend `control`; it must never remove or narrow a built-in entry.\n    88\t`.forge/evals/candidates/**` is the sole eval-path exception: classify it as advisory/docs-class,\n    89\tnot `control`, even when an older or broader project `control` pattern matches it. Moving or copying\n    90\ta candidate into `.forge/evals/tasks/**`, or creating or changing its baseline there, is a\n    91\tcontrol-class promotion.\n    92\tFail closed if a changed path cannot be classified. Keep `CANDIDATE_HEAD` unchanged through Gates\n    93\t1 through 4. If HEAD or the diff changes, restart at the clean-worktree precondition.\n    94\t\n    95\tDerive merge-tier evidence mechanically from this exact candidate range and committed policy:\n    96\t\n    97\t```bash\n    98\tdeclared_tier=\"${declared_tier:-}\"\n    99\tdeclared_args=()\n   100\tif [ -n \"$declared_tier\" ]; then\n   101\t  case \"$declared_tier\" in\n   102\t    fast|standard|hard) declared_args=(--declared-tier \"$declared_tier\") ;;\n   103\t    *) echo \"forge: invalid declared risk tier: $declared_tier\" >&2; exit 1 ;;\n   104\t  esac\n   105\tfi\n   106\tTIER_EVIDENCE=\"$(python3 \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/forge/risk_tier.py\" \\\n   107\t  --repo \"$PWD\" --policy-sha \"$policy_sha\" \"${declared_args[@]}\" \\\n   108\t  --range \"${REVIEWED_BASE}...${CANDIDATE_HEAD}\")\" || exit 1\n   109\t```\n   110\t\n   111\tIf the task/journal supplies a declared/decomposed tier, set `declared_tier` to that exact\n   112\t`fast`, `standard`, or `hard` value before this block. Otherwise omit the advisory declaration;\n   113\tnever pass an empty or invented tier.\n   114\t\n   115\tThe compact JSON evidence must retain the exact path list, matched tier/trigger/category rows,\n     1\t# Refactor plan — 2026-09-19\n     2\t\n     3\tStatus: **historical protocol record, not authority.** This note records the operator-directed\n     4\tworking protocol of the 2026-09-19..22 decomposition sessions (Engine, MergeEngine). Two of its\n     5\trules were session-scoped operator directions that deviate from the committed repository rules\n     6\tand were accepted as such at reintegration (review finding OPS-03 on `657f6c1`): authoring the\n     7\trefactor branch with the Forge plugin disabled, and admitting 500–1,000-line modules through\n     8\tprovisional `.refactor-baseline.json` entries. Neither is a standing permission. Wherever this\n     9\tnote conflicts with `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` — every commit through the Forge commit chain,\n    10\tno Python file over 500 code lines, baseline entries grandfathered-only — the committed rules\n    11\tgovern, and every branch this protocol produced was reintegrated through the Forge\n    12\tworktree-merge chain with its four gates.\n    13\t\n    14\tPoint of reference for the decomposition sessions that work through\n    49\t## 2. Session protocol\n    50\t\n    51\t### Start checklist (the session runs these, the bead tells it to)\n    52\t\n    53\t`$S` below is the `scripts/` directory of the refactor-python plugin's `split-module` skill\n    54\t(locally `~/foundry-of-zero/refactor-python/skills/split-module/scripts`). The mint script named\n    55\tin step 5 lives under `.codex-orchestrator/runs/`, which is per-clone (`info/exclude`) — the\n    56\tchecklist is reproducible only on a machine that holds that run directory.\n    57\t\n    58\t1. `cat .claude/settings.local.json` shows `\"forge@forge\": false`. If not, set it and note it\n    59\t   for the end checklist. No `/forge:*` skills, chains, markers or approvals during the session.\n    60\t2. `git status` clean on `main` at the tip named in the bead; `git switch -c refactor/<name>`.\n    74\t### During\n    75\t\n    76\t- Freeze (bodies, test ids where tests are touched, type baseline), inventory, plan, critique,\n    77\t  then one cluster at a time, sequential per source file. Dry run, then `--apply`, always with\n    78\t  `--format-imports` (this repository enforces isort); function-shape method moves also pass\n    79\t  `--annotate-self` and stop on NEW or LOST mypy keys.\n    80\t- Per-cluster snapshot scope must equal the gate's `--pkg` path. Keep all evidence under\n    81\t  tracked `.refactor/` with unique names.\n    82\t- Never include Ruff `I001` in destination per-file ignores or globs; temporary globs for\n    83\t  relocated complexity codes are replaced by measured per-module entries at finalize.\n    84\t- Never hand-edit a body. A refusal is a planning result: re-plan or report, never bypass.\n    85\t- Tier 1 (relocation) and tier 2 (declared extraction) never share a commit. Tier 3 is not\n    86\t  in this plan.\n    87\t- FR-230: production subjects are byte-pinned. Add every new module under a subject package\n    88\t  to the manifest, run `verify.sh --mint` at wave close and finalize, commit the manifest,\n    89\t  `tests/fixtures/fr230-results/*.json` and the byte pin with the wave. Keep the digest tests\n    90\t  out of the focused per-cluster set.\n    91\t- Layout pins (patch targets, `__globals__` identity, plain assignments in fixtures) are\n    92\t  repointed in the same commit as the move under the operator's standing permission.\n    93\t  Behaviour tests are never edited. Class-patch sites keep working under function-shape\n    94\t  bindings and need no repoint; confirm with the census output.\n    95\t- `__all__` verbatim from baseline to finalize. CHANGELOG: one entry per branch.\n    96\t\n    97\t### End checklist\n    98\t\n    99\t1. Finalize: measured `.refactor-baseline.json` (old entry gone or shrunk, provisional\n   100\t   entries only for modules the plan marked over target), `lint-imports` contract, spec\n   101\t   line 117 wording if a package layout changed, re-mint, gate-1 cell twice consecutively.\n   102\t2. Codex review detached, then the Fable reviewer adjudicates; consensus round on disagreement.\n   103\t3. Debt report: every module between 500 and 1,000, every function over 150 lines, every\n   104\t   class over 30 methods, each with reason and follow-up bead.\n   105\t4. Handover bead in the style of forge-plugin-90b0: branch, tip SHA, old-to-new path map,\n   106\t   every non-move edit, expected gates, debt report. Push the branch. Reintegration is a\n   107\t   separate Forge session.\n   108\t5. Restore `.claude/settings.local.json` to `\"forge@forge\": true`. Remove the run's\n     1\t# Consensus round: Engine decompose reviews (2026-09-20)\n     2\t\n     3\tReviewed tip: 813246a (base main 7e40590). Codex (gpt-5.6-sol, effort ultra, thread\n     4\t01a0c00d-7844-7fa1-93f6-c89a33b6cadb): REJECT with 3 BLOCKING + 4 ADVISORY\n     5\t(`codex-review-engine-class.md`). Fable refactor-reviewer: APPROVE, no blocking; every Codex item\n     6\tCONFIRMED as fact, B1-B3 REFUTED as blocking (`fable-review-engine-class.md`). Follow-ups on the Codex\n     7\tthread, one per disputed finding:\n     8\t\n     9\t| finding | Codex answer | record |\n    10\t|---|---|---|\n    11\t| B1 wrapped class functions no longer pickle | AGREE: advisory for the handover (no consumer; operations.md permits it for function shape) | `consensus-engine-class-B1.md` |\n    12\t| B2 temporary glob retained PLR0904 | AGREE: no applicable rule occurrence was masked (no class in any verb module); plan deviation is a handover advisory | `consensus-engine-class-B2.md` |\n    13\t| B3 cluster commits without a CHANGELOG line | AGREE: cluster commits complied with the governing one-entry-per-branch protocol; conflict with the planner's text is a handover advisory | `consensus-engine-class-B3.md` |\n    14\t\n    15\tOutcome: no blocking finding stands. Advisories carried to the handover: pickling / `__qualname__` /\n    16\t`__module__` change of the 18 wrapped class functions (and 3 staticmethod bindings); ten lost mypy checks\n    17\t(bead forge-plugin-psvo); `_engine` no longer binds 71 imported globals (private module, no reader);\n    18\tthe operator's 2026-09-19 direction that the temporary glob carry the `_engine.py` code list (then minus\n    19\tI001, 5025042) is not worded as operator direction in the commit messages; the plan's per-commit CHANGELOG\n    20\twording was not amended to the protocol's one entry per branch; \"tree identical\" in the plan means\n    21\tsource-identical (5480091 adds only .refactor-quality.json); the nine verb modules lack a terminal newline\n    22\t(operator decision pending at the time of this record).\n     1\tAGREE\n     2\t\n     3\t`.claude/settings.local.json:19-20` disables `forge@forge`, while `docs/analysis/refactor-plan-2026-09-19.md:42-43` explicitly prohibits Forge chains during the split, line 73 requires “CHANGELOG: one entry per branch,” and lines 83-85 defer Forge reintegration to a separate session. `git show --stat 78d9610` confirms the branch entry was added with the setup commit, and `git show 813246a:CHANGELOG.md | nl -ba` shows the finalized entry at line 13. Thus the cluster commits complied with the governing branch protocol; their conflict with `.refactor/plan-engine-class.md` should be disclosed as an advisory, not treated as a blocking gate failure.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
